ints (-34.6 to -45.6). The engine's choice was A4. With the lead already past -30, this pushed the game further out of reach."}, {"turn": 49, "text": "G1 was the worst move of the game, losing 35.3 points and dropping the lead from -46.7 to -82.0. The engine's choice was F1. Black's stones were already on G2 and H2 beside White's H1, and the bottom edge turned out to be the most dangerous place on the board."}, {"turn": 52, "text": "The 14k answered with D1 (30.7 points lost) and then C1, which lost 34.7 points and moved the lead from -83.7 to -49.0. The engine wanted J8 both times. The two errors cancelled out, but Black was still behind by about 49 points, and Opus 5.5 resigned after move 54."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints groups with their liberties, and count.py only tallies area for the current position; the other commands just read or append to games.md. None of them chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}